{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`.github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml:68-184,397` invokes external actions in a workflow with contents/actions-write and OIDC capability. Existing actionlint covers all workflows, but `Makefile` does not require zizmor to inspect this credentialed workflow and the focused pin contract covers only release workflow behavior.\n\n## Approach\n\nReplace every non-relative/external `uses:` reference in `.github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml`—including `actions/checkout`, `actions/setup-python`, and `actions/cache`, as well as third-party actions—with an exact 40-hex commit SHA followed by a readable version comment. Edit `Makefile` so `ZIZMOR_WORKFLOWS` unconditionally includes `.github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml`. Extend `tests/unit/test_release_workflow_pins.py` (or its renamed focused successor) by reading each complete external `uses:` line, not its existing whitespace-truncated `uses:\\s*(\\S+)` token. Match the complete line against `uses:\\s*\\S+@([0-9a-f]{40})\\s+#\\s+[^\\n]+$`, thereby proving both the SHA and its trailing readable version comment.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `.github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml`\n- `Makefile` — add the workflow to `ZIZMOR_WORKFLOWS`.\n- `tests/unit/test_release_workflow_pins.py` — parse complete external `uses:` lines and enforce the full-SHA-plus-readable-version-comment contract.\n\n## Testing\n\nRun the focused pin test with three negative controls: a mutable tag, a bare SHA without a comment, and a SHA followed by a comment that the whitespace-token extractor would otherwise discard. Run the existing `make lint` actionlint/zizmor path and confirm zizmor receives the reconciliation workflow.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Every external `uses:` reference in `.github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml`, including first-party `actions/*`, has an exact 40-hex SHA followed by a readable version comment.\n- [ ] `Makefile` unconditionally includes `.github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml` in `ZIZMOR_WORKFLOWS`.\n- [ ] The focused pin test reads complete `uses:` lines and fails for a mutable tag, a bare SHA, and an unexamined trailing comment; it does not reuse a whitespace-truncated token to verify the comment.\n- [ ] The focused test and existing actionlint/zizmor checks pass with the pinned workflow.","title":"SHA-pin all external actions in the privileged reconciliation workflow"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788323754945280001,"uuid":"2b40372a-e32b-44b8-aed2-ed20efd55ca3"}